codex
Both bridge layers fire on symbolic standalone states but not when the module and builtin maps are concrete. The mismatch is the exact three-entry map decomposition, not the execution term. Since the loop reads only its complete local frame at key `1` and the rule preserves every other scope, I’m generalizing all supporting theorems and bridges to `SC:Map` plus that exact local entry. This enlarges the theorem and bridge identically while preserving the full state footprint.
apply patch
