codex
The final Gate A inventory found one avoidable issue: the source-level bridge’s connection theorem depended on the already connected `#while` bridge, so it was not strictly bridge-free. Now that the true singleton-`Stmts` continuation is known, the entry proof can use only the `#while` bridge. I’m removing the redundant source bridge, rebuilding, and re-running the full audit so the sole operational bridge has a genuinely bridge-free universal theorem.
